INT. ER TRAUMA BAY 3 - NIGHT

Harsh white light. Stainless steel. A monitor beeps too fast. Blood on the floor tiles, smeared by a gurney's wheels.

DR. PRIYA RAMASWAMY (40s, surgical cap, steady) leans over a patient. NURSE CALEB DUNMORE (30s, tattooed forearms) squeezes a bag valve. RESIDENT DR. INGRID SOLBERG (20s, pale and wide-eyed) hovers at the foot of the bed. On the table lies MR. OTIS WEBB (70s), unconscious, his shirt cut open.

PRIYA
Pressure?

CALEB
Seventy over forty.

PRIYA
Ingrid, give me two units of O neg.

INGRID
Right away, Dr. Ramaswamy.

PRIYA
Priya. Please. Just Priya.

PARAMEDIC GUS TREMAINE (30s, soaked jacket) bursts in, still holding a clipboard.

GUS
Dr. Priya! Wife says he took nitro an hour ago!

CALEB
He's crashing.

The monitor flatlines. A long, flat tone.

PRIYA
Charge to two hundred.

CALEB
Charging.

PRIYA
Clear!

The body jerks. The line stays flat.

PRIYA (CONT'D)
Again. Three hundred.

INGRID
Dr. Priya --

PRIYA
Now, Ingrid!

Another shock. A blip. Another. A steady rhythm.

CALEB
We have a pulse.

Ingrid exhales. Priya wipes her forehead with a gloved wrist.
